# 2026-08-13 11:28:46.639198
+Create a new file called BioComputeGrid.jsx with the following spec: # Bio-Compute Grid — Interactive 3D Portfolio Prompt
+
+Act as an expert Creative Technologist and Senior React / Three.js Developer.
+Generate a COMPLETE, fully functional, interactive 3D portfolio website in a single React component file (using `@react-three/fiber`, `@react-three/drei`, `@react-three/postprocessing`, `three`, `framer-motion`, `lucide-react`, and `Tailwind CSS`).
+Do NOT leave placeholders, `// TODO` comments, or incomplete sections. Write the entire working code — every geometry, shader, and animation loop fully implemented.
+
+---
+
+## Visual Concept & Theme: "Bio-Compute Grid"
+
+- **Aesthetic**: High-tech dark mode merging High-Performance Computing (HPC) nodes with biological structures (DNA/Bioinformatics).
+- **Color Palette**: Dark Slate/Obsidian background (`#0b0f19`), Electric Cyan (`#00f2fe`), Bio-Green/Emerald (`#10b981`), Cool Metallic accents (`#94a3b8`).
+- **Post-processing stack** (via `@react-three/postprocessing`): `Bloom` (intensity tuned to make the cyan/emerald emissive materials glow), `ChromaticAberration` (subtle, offset-based on camera velocity), `Vignette`, and `Noise` (very low opacity, film-grain feel).
+
+---
+
+## Interactive 3D Scene Features
+
+### 1. Central 3D Model — Animated Double Helix in a Server Ring
+
+- Procedurally generated DNA double helix: two intertwined strands built from instanced spheres or tubes (`<Tube>` / `TubeGeometry` along a sine/cosine parametric curve), with connecting "base pair" rungs as thin cylinders, color-alternating cyan/emerald.
+- The helix continuously rotates on its own axis (`useFrame`) independent of user interaction, with a secondary subtle vertical bob (sine wave on `position.y`).
+- Surrounding "server rack ring": a torus or ring of instanced boxes (`InstancedMesh`) styled as blade-server units, each with emissive edges (`meshStandardMaterial` with `emissive` + `emissiveIntensity` driven by a per-instance offset sine wave, simulating asynchronous "blinking LED" activity).
+- Use custom GLSL shaders (`shaderMaterial` via drei's `shaderMaterial` helper) for at least one surface — e.g., a Fresnel/rim-glow shader on the helix strands, or a scanline/data-flow shader (UV-animated scrolling gradient) on the ring — so the glow isn't just emissive color but an actual custom fragment shader effect.
+
+### 2. Camera & Interaction Choreography
+
+- `OrbitControls` with `enableZoom={false}`, `enablePan={false}`, damped rotation (`enableDamping`, `dampingFactor`), and rotation clamped to a believable range (`minPolarAngle` / `maxPolarAngle`) so the model can't be flipped upside down.
+- Mouse-driven parallax: on top of OrbitControls' drag rotation, the whole scene group subtly offsets/rotates toward normalized mouse position when NOT actively dragging, using `useFrame` + `lerp` for smoothing (three's `MathUtils.lerp`), so it feels alive even without interaction.
+- "Explore Compute Grid" CTA button triggers a scripted camera dolly-zoom: animate `camera.position` and `camera.fov` via `useFrame` + `gsap`-free `framer-motion`-driven state (or a simple lerp-to-target pattern) that pushes the camera in close to the helix core, then pulls back to reveal the full scene as the page auto-scrolls to the About section. Implement this as a real state machine (`idle` → `zooming-in` → `settled`), not a CSS transition.
+- Scroll-linked camera movement: as the user scrolls past Skills/Projects sections, use `useScroll` (drei) or a scroll-progress hook to subtly rotate/reposition the 3D group so it feels tethered to page content, not just a static hero background.
+
+### 3. Floating Particle Field — Cluster Compute Nodes
+
+- Custom `InstancedMesh` or `Points`-based particle system (hundreds of instances) representing compute nodes / molecular data points, distributed in a spherical volume around the central model.
+- Each particle has: individual drift velocity (simple noise-based movement, e.g., a per-particle seed feeding `Math.sin`/`Math.cos` offsets in `useFrame`), slow color interpolation between cyan and emerald (`Color.lerpColors`), and subtle size pulsing.
+- Mouse-repel interaction: particles within a radius of the projected mouse/raycast position gently push away and drift back (spring-like return, e.g. lerp toward home position when not disturbed) — this should use actual raycasting against an invisible plane, not just 2D CSS.
+
+### 4. Dynamic Lighting
+
+- `ambientLight` (low intensity, cool tone), one `directionalLight` acting as key light, and a `pointLight` whose position is updated every frame to track the raycasted cursor position in 3D space, with color cycling subtly between cyan and emerald based on time.
+- Optional: a rim/back `pointLight` fixed behind the helix for silhouette definition.
+
+### 5. Performance & Robustness
+
+- Wrap the Canvas content in `<Suspense fallback={null}>`.
+- Use `dpr={[1, 2]}` and `performance={{ min: 0.5 }}` on the `<Canvas>` for adaptive quality.
+- All `useFrame` callbacks must avoid allocating new objects/vectors per frame (reuse refs/`Vector3` instances) to keep this performant.
+
+---
+
+## User Interface & Content Sections
+
+### 1. Header / Navigation
+
+- Floating glassmorphism navbar (`backdrop-blur`, semi-transparent slate, subtle border-glow) with smooth-scroll links ("About", "Skills", "Projects", "Contact"), active-section highlighting driven by scroll position (`IntersectionObserver`).
+- Interactive theme badge / status indicator: an animated pulsing dot (framer-motion `animate` loop) labeled "System Online" or similar, reinforcing the HPC theme.
+
+### 2. Hero Section
+
+- **Name**: Maneesh B
+- **Headline**: "Machine Learning & High-Performance Computing (HPC) | Computational Biology"
+- **Location**: Kasaragod, Kerala, India | SSSIHL
+- **Interactive Elements**:
+  - "Explore Compute Grid" CTA button that triggers the camera dolly-zoom described above and scrolls to About.
+  - Direct link to GitHub (`https://github.com/maneesh22122005-hub/biopulse-hud-agar-analytics`), styled as an icon-button with hover glow (`lucide-react` GitHub icon).
+- Hero text uses `framer-motion` staggered entrance animation (fade + slide) on mount.
+
+### 3. Interactive Skills Grid (3D Glass Cards)
+
+Hover-responsive glass cards (CSS 3D tilt via `framer-motion`'s `useMotionValue` + `useTransform` tracking mouse position over each card, not just a flat `scale` hover) featuring:
+
+- **Computational Biology & Bioinformatics** — sequence processing, structural analysis, statistical modeling (Python, R)
+- **High-Performance Computing (HPC)** — SLURM workload manager, Linux shell, cluster scheduling & scaling
+- **Machine Learning & AI** — model training, distributed data preprocessing, predictive analytics
+
+Each card has an animated gradient border on hover and a subtle "scan line" sweep effect (CSS keyframe or framer-motion animate).
+
+### 4. Featured Project Highlight
+
+- Interactive project showcase card for **BioPulse HUD & Agar Analytics**.
+- Dynamic tech tags (Python, R, SLURM, Bio-Analytics) as pill badges.
+- Direct GitHub repo link button.
+- Interactive preview box: an animated mock "terminal/HUD" panel (fake scrolling log lines or a simple canvas-based waveform/graph placeholder built from actual SVG/CSS, not an image) that idles with subtle motion to suggest a live dashboard.
+
+### 5. Footer & Contact CTA
+
+- Interactive contact banner: "Open to research collaborations and discussions around ML Infrastructure, HPC, and Scalable AI."
+- One-click copy-email button using the Clipboard API, with a visual confirmation state (icon swap to checkmark + toast/tooltip via `framer-motion`, auto-reverting after ~2s).
+
+---
+
+## Code Requirements
+
+- Return full React code starting with standard imports (`import React, { useRef, useState, useMemo, useEffect } from 'react'`, plus all R3F/drei/postprocessing/framer-motion/lucide-react imports).
+- All custom shaders must be complete, valid GLSL strings embedded via drei's `shaderMaterial`, registered with `extend()`.
+- All Three.js geometries/materials must use real, valid `@react-three/fiber` JSX primitives (`<sphereGeometry>`, `<meshStandardMaterial>`, `<instancedMesh>`, etc.) — no invented components.
+- Wrap the whole app in a responsive, mobile-aware layout using Tailwind CSS (verify the 3D canvas gracefully degrades or resizes on small viewports — cap particle/instance counts on narrow screens).
+- Single file, fully self-contained, ready to drop into a Vite/CRA React project with the listed dependencies installed.

