+- **Scroll-linked animation smoothing**: scroll-driven camera/UI changes (the scroll-linked camera movement, active-nav-link highlighting) should be smoothed/interpolated rather than snapping directly to scroll position — lerp the displayed value toward the scroll-derived target each frame so fast scrolling doesn't cause jarring jumps.
+- **Hover/tap micro-interactions**: buttons, cards, and icon-links should have subtle, quick eased transitions on hover/tap (scale, glow-intensity, border-gradient shift) — around 150–300ms with an ease-out curve — so interactions feel responsive but not abrupt.
+- **No competing/conflicting animations**: ensure state-machine-driven animations (like the camera dolly-zoom `idle → zooming-in → settled`) fully own their target values while active, so they don't fight with the idle parallax/drift animations running in the same frame loop — gate or blend between them explicitly rather than letting both write to the same transform simultaneously.
+
+---
+
+## Code Requirements
+
+- Return full React code starting with standard imports (`import React, { useRef, useState, useMemo, useEffect } from 'react'`, plus all R3F/drei/postprocessing/framer-motion/lucide-react imports).
+- All custom shaders must be complete, valid GLSL strings embedded via drei's `shaderMaterial`, registered with `extend()`.
+- All Three.js geometries/materials must use real, valid `@react-three/fiber` JSX primitives (`<sphereGeometry>`, `<meshStandardMaterial>`, `<instancedMesh>`, etc.) — no invented components.
+- Wrap the whole app in a responsive, mobile-aware layout using Tailwind CSS (verify the 3D canvas gracefully degrades or resizes on small viewports — cap particle/instance counts on narrow screens).
+- Single file, fully self-contained, ready to drop into a Vite/CRA React project with the listed dependencies installed.

